module

public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Quotient
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The ideal cutting out the base changes on which a map into a flat module vanishes

Let `R` be a commutative ring, let `A` be an `R`-algebra and let `u : M ⟶ N` be a map of
`A`-modules whose target is flat as an `R`-module.  Let `R'` be an `R`-algebra and suppose the
base change `u ⊗_R R'` vanishes.  This file produces an ideal `I ⊆ R` which maps to zero in
`R'` and for which the base change `u ⊗_R R/I` already vanishes; when `M` is a finite
`A`-module the ideal can be taken finitely generated.

The ideal is simply the kernel of `R ⟶ R'`, and flatness of the target is what makes it work:
`R/\ker \subseteq R'` is injective, so tensoring with the flat module `N` keeps it injective,
and an element of `N` dying in `N ⊗_R R'` therefore already dies in `N ⊗_R R/\ker = N/\ker N`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Flattening.mem_ker_smul_top_of_tmul_eq_zero`: an element of a flat `R`-module which
  dies in the base change to `R'` lies in `\ker(R ⟶ R') \cdot N`.
* `Stacks.Flattening.exists_fg_le_ker_mem_smul_top`: the finitely generated refinement — the
  element already lies in `J \cdot N` for a finitely generated ideal `J ⊆ \ker(R ⟶ R')`.
* `Stacks.Flattening.tmul_eq_zero_of_forall_tmul_eq_zero` and
  `Stacks.Flattening.tmul_one_eq_zero_of_forall_tmul_one_eq_zero`: a flat module detects the
  vanishing of `n ⊗ 1` through a *finite* family of base changes into which the given one
  injects.
* `Stacks.Flattening.rTensor_quotient_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top`: a map whose values lie in
  `J \cdot N` has vanishing base change to `R/J`.
* `Stacks.Flattening.rTensor_quotient_ker_eq_zero`: the main statement — the base change of `u`
  to `R/\ker(R ⟶ R')` vanishes.
* `Stacks.Flattening.exists_fg_ideal_rTensor_quotient_eq_zero`: the finitely generated
  refinement for a map out of a finite `A`-module.
* `Stacks.Flattening.lTensor_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top` and
  `Stacks.Flattening.lTensor_eq_zero_of_rTensor_eq_zero`: the base change of `u` to *any*
  `A`-module on which the ideal acts by zero vanishes.

## Implementation notes

This is the commutative-algebra content of the affine case of Stacks 083K, in which `R` is the
ring of the affine base `S = Spec(R)`, `A` is the ring of an affine chart of the algebraic
space `X`, `M` and `N` are the modules of `\mathcal{F}` and `\mathcal{G}` on that chart, `R'` is
the ring of an affine test scheme `T = Spec(R')` over `S`, and the ideal `I` cuts out the closed
subscheme `Z = Spec(R/I) ⊆ S` the tag asks for.  Nothing here carries the tag: 083K is a
statement about a map of quasi-coherent modules on an algebraic space and about a closed
subscheme of its base, and neither the space nor the subscheme appears below.

The source's proof of the affine case takes `I` to be generated by the coordinates of lifts of
the elements `u(z)` through free `R`-modules, which Lazard's theorem
(`Stacks.RingTheory.flat_iff_directLimit_free_finite`, Tag 058G) supplies.  The ideal produced
here is the larger `\ker(R ⟶ R')`, which cuts out the *smallest* closed subscheme through which
`T ⟶ S` factors and therefore satisfies the tag's two requirements equally; the resulting proof
needs only that a flat module preserves the injection `R/\ker(R ⟶ R') ↪ R'`.  The finitely
generated refinement does need a choice of generators, but only of the finitely many elements
`u(z)` for `z` in a generating set of `M`, each of which is a finite sum `\sum a_i \cdot n_i`
with `a_i ∈ \ker(R ⟶ R')`; the `a_i` generate the finitely generated ideal.

The source reduces a quasi-compact test scheme `T` to an affine one by replacing it with the
coproduct of a finite affine open covering, whose ring of functions is the product of the rings
of the members.  `Stacks.Flattening.tmul_one_eq_zero_of_forall_tmul_one_eq_zero` achieves the
same reduction without forming the coproduct, and with `R' = \Gamma(T)` itself rather than the
product: flatness of `N` keeps the injection `\Gamma(T) ↪ \prod_j \Gamma(T_j)` injective after
tensoring, the index set is finite so the target tensors to the product of the factors, and the
element `n ⊗ 1` therefore dies in `N ⊗_R \Gamma(T)` as soon as it dies in each
`N ⊗_R \Gamma(T_j)`.  Taking `R' = \Gamma(T)` is what makes the factorisation of `T ⟶ S`
through `\Spec(R/\ker(R ⟶ R'))` immediate.

The `R`-module structures on `M` and `N` are the restrictions along `R ⟶ A`, expressed by
`[Module R M] [IsScalarTower R A M]` rather than by `Module.compHom`, so that the statements
compose with Mathlib's tensor API.  The set of elements of `N` lying in `J \cdot N` for an ideal
`J` of `R` is an `A`-submodule, `Stacks.Flattening.smulTopOfTower`, because the two scalar
actions commute; that is what lets a generating set of `M` over `A` suffice.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 083K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/083K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 058G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/058G)
-/

@[expose] public section

open TensorProduct

namespace Stacks.Flattening

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {R' : Type*} [CommRing R'] [Algebra R R']

/-! ### Elements of a flat module killed by a base change -/

section Flat

variable {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N]

/-- An element of `J • N` dies in `N ⊗_R Q` whenever `J` annihilates `Q`. -/
theorem tmul_eq_zero_of_mem_smul_top {J : Ideal R} {Q : Type*} [AddCommGroup Q] [Module R Q]
    (hQ : ∀ a ∈ J, ∀ q : Q, a • q = 0) {n : N} (hn : n ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N)) (q : Q) :
    n ⊗ₜ[R] q = 0 :=
  Submodule.smul_induction_on hn
    (fun a ha x _ => by rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul, hQ a ha q, tmul_zero])
    (fun x y hx hy => by rw [add_tmul, hx, hy, add_zero])

/-- An ideal annihilates the quotient of the ring by it. -/
theorem smul_quotient_eq_zero (J : Ideal R) {a : R} (ha : a ∈ J) (q : R ⧸ J) : a • q = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ q
  rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, smul_eq_mul]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ ha

/-- An element `n` of `N` with `n ⊗ 1 = 0` in `N ⊗_R R/J` lies in `J • N`. -/
private theorem mem_smul_top_of_tmul_one_eq_zero {J : Ideal R} {n : N}
    (h : n ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : R ⧸ J) = 0) : n ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N) := by
  have := congrArg (TensorProduct.tensorQuotEquivQuotSMul N J) h
  rw [map_zero, TensorProduct.tensorQuotEquivQuotSMul, LinearEquiv.trans_apply,
    TensorProduct.comm_tmul, TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul_mk_one_tmul] at this
  exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero _).mp this

/-- **An element of a flat module which dies in a base change lies in the kernel ideal times
the module.**  If `n ⊗ 1` vanishes in `N ⊗_R R'`, then `n` lies in `\ker(R ⟶ R') \cdot N`. -/
theorem mem_ker_smul_top_of_tmul_eq_zero [Module.Flat R N] {n : N}
    (h : n ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : R') = 0) :
    n ∈ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R')) • (⊤ : Submodule R N) := by
  set I : Ideal R := RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R') with hI
  have hle : (I : Submodule R R) ≤ LinearMap.ker (Algebra.linearMap R R') := fun a ha => ha
  -- the `R`-linear injection `R/I ↪ R'`
  set q : (R ⧸ I) →ₗ[R] R' := (I : Submodule R R).liftQ (Algebra.linearMap R R') hle with hq
  have hqinj : Function.Injective q := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot, hq, Submodule.ker_liftQ_eq_bot']
    rfl
  -- flatness keeps it injective after tensoring with `N`
  have hinj : Function.Injective (q.lTensor N) :=
    Module.Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap q hqinj
  have hz : n ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : R ⧸ I) = 0 := by
    refine hinj ?_
    rw [map_zero, LinearMap.lTensor_tmul]
    show n ⊗ₜ[R] q (Ideal.Quotient.mk I 1) = 0
    rwa [show q (Ideal.Quotient.mk I 1) = (1 : R') from map_one (algebraMap R R')]
  -- and `N ⊗_R R/I` is `N/IN`
  exact mem_smul_top_of_tmul_one_eq_zero hz

/-- **The finitely generated refinement.**  An element of a flat module which dies in a base
change already lies in `J \cdot N` for a finitely generated ideal `J` contained in the kernel of
the base-change map. -/
theorem exists_fg_le_ker_mem_smul_top [Module.Flat R N] {n : N} (h : n ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : R') = 0) :
    ∃ J : Ideal R, J.FG ∧ J ≤ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R') ∧
      n ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N) := by
  have hn := mem_ker_smul_top_of_tmul_eq_zero (R' := R') h
  refine Submodule.smul_induction_on hn (fun a ha x _ => ?_) (fun x y hx hy => ?_)
  · refine ⟨Ideal.span {a}, Submodule.fg_span_singleton a, ?_, ?_⟩
    · exact (Ideal.span_le).2 (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 ha)
    · exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self a) Submodule.mem_top
  · obtain ⟨J₁, hJ₁fg, hJ₁le, hx'⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨J₂, hJ₂fg, hJ₂le, hy'⟩ := hy
    refine ⟨J₁ ⊔ J₂, Submodule.FG.sup hJ₁fg hJ₂fg, sup_le hJ₁le hJ₂le, add_mem ?_ ?_⟩
    · exact Submodule.smul_mono_left le_sup_left hx'
    · exact Submodule.smul_mono_left le_sup_right hy'

/-! #### Assembling finitely many base changes -/

/-- **A flat module detects vanishing through a finite family of maps that are jointly
injective.**  Let `f i : P ⟶ Q i` be `R`-linear maps, with `i` ranging over a finite type, such
that an element of `P` killed by every `f i` is zero.  If `n ⊗ f i p` vanishes for every `i`,
then `n ⊗ p` already vanishes. -/
theorem tmul_eq_zero_of_forall_tmul_eq_zero [Module.Flat R N] {P : Type*} [AddCommGroup P]
    [Module R P] {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {Q : ι → Type*} [∀ i, AddCommGroup (Q i)]
    [∀ i, Module R (Q i)] (f : ∀ i, P →ₗ[R] Q i)
    (hf : ∀ p : P, (∀ i, f i p = 0) → p = 0) {n : N} {p : P}
    (h : ∀ i, n ⊗ₜ[R] f i p = 0) :
    n ⊗ₜ[R] p = 0 := by
  classical
  have hinj : Function.Injective (LinearMap.pi f) := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot]
    refine LinearMap.ker_eq_bot'.2 fun x hx => hf x fun i => ?_
    simpa using congrFun hx i
  refine Module.Flat.lTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap (M := N) (LinearMap.pi f) hinj ?_
  rw [map_zero, LinearMap.lTensor_tmul]
  show n ⊗ₜ[R] (fun i => f i p) = 0
  rw [← Finset.univ_sum_single (fun i => f i p), TensorProduct.tmul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun i _ => ?_
  calc n ⊗ₜ[R] Pi.single i (f i p)
      = (LinearMap.lTensor N (LinearMap.single R Q i)) (n ⊗ₜ[R] f i p) := by
        rw [LinearMap.lTensor_tmul]; rfl
    _ = 0 := by rw [h i, map_zero]

/-- **The unit of a flat module dies in a base change as soon as it dies in each member of a
finite family through which that base change injects.**  If `R'` is an `R`-algebra mapping to
finitely many `R`-algebras `Rj i` so that an element of `R'` vanishing in every `Rj i` is zero,
and `n ⊗ 1` vanishes in `N ⊗_R Rj i` for every `i`, then `n ⊗ 1` vanishes in `N ⊗_R R'`.

Geometrically `R'` is the ring of global functions on a quasi-compact scheme `T` over
`\Spec(R)` and the `Rj i` are the rings of a finite affine open covering of `T`: the structure
sheaf is separated, so a function vanishing on each member of the covering is zero. -/
@[ega "IV 11.10.5" "(ii)(a), special case", ega "IV 11.9.10" "(ii)(a), special case"]
theorem tmul_one_eq_zero_of_forall_tmul_one_eq_zero [Module.Flat R N] {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
    {Rj : ι → Type*} [∀ i, CommRing (Rj i)] [∀ i, Algebra R (Rj i)] (φ : ∀ i, R' →ₐ[R] Rj i)
    (hφ : ∀ x : R', (∀ i, φ i x = 0) → x = 0) {n : N} (h : ∀ i, n ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : Rj i) = 0) :
    n ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : R') = 0 :=
  tmul_eq_zero_of_forall_tmul_eq_zero (fun i => (φ i).toLinearMap) hφ
    (fun i => by simpa using h i)

end Flat

/-! ### Vanishing of the base change to a quotient of the base ring -/

section Map

variable {M N : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N]

/-- If the base change of `u` to `Q` vanishes, then `u m ⊗ q = 0` for all `m` and `q`. -/
private theorem tmul_eq_zero_of_rTensor_eq_zero {Q : Type*} [AddCommGroup Q] [Module R Q]
    (u : M →ₗ[R] N) (h : LinearMap.rTensor Q u = 0) (m : M) (q : Q) : u m ⊗ₜ[R] q = 0 := by
  rw [← LinearMap.rTensor_tmul, h]; rfl

/-- A map all of whose values lie in `J • N` has vanishing base change to `R/J`. -/
theorem rTensor_quotient_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top {J : Ideal R} (u : M →ₗ[R] N)
    (h : ∀ m : M, u m ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N)) :
    LinearMap.rTensor (R ⧸ J) u = 0 := by
  refine TensorProduct.ext' fun m z => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.rTensor_tmul]
  exact tmul_eq_zero_of_mem_smul_top (fun a ha => smul_quotient_eq_zero J ha) (h m) z

/-- A map has vanishing base change to `R/J` if and only if all of its values lie in `J • N`. -/
theorem rTensor_quotient_eq_zero_iff_forall_mem_smul_top {J : Ideal R} (u : M →ₗ[R] N) :
    LinearMap.rTensor (R ⧸ J) u = 0 ↔ ∀ m : M, u m ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N) := by
  refine ⟨fun h m => ?_, rTensor_quotient_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top u⟩
  exact mem_smul_top_of_tmul_one_eq_zero (tmul_eq_zero_of_rTensor_eq_zero u h m 1)

/-- **The ring-level core of Stacks 083K.**  If the target of an `R`-linear map is flat over `R`
and the base change of the map to an `R`-algebra `R'` vanishes, then its base change to
`R/\ker(R ⟶ R')` already vanishes.

Geometrically: `Spec(R/\ker(R ⟶ R')) ⊆ Spec(R)` is a closed subscheme through which
`Spec(R') ⟶ Spec(R)` factors, and the map becomes zero on it. -/
theorem rTensor_quotient_ker_eq_zero [Module.Flat R N] (u : M →ₗ[R] N)
    (h : LinearMap.rTensor R' u = 0) :
    LinearMap.rTensor (R ⧸ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R')) u = 0 := by
  refine rTensor_quotient_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top u fun m => ?_
  exact mem_ker_smul_top_of_tmul_eq_zero (R' := R') (tmul_eq_zero_of_rTensor_eq_zero u h m 1)

end Map

/-! ### The finitely generated ideal for a map out of a finite module -/

section Tower

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
variable {M N : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module A M] [IsScalarTower R A M]
  [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [Module A N] [IsScalarTower R A N]

/-- For an ideal `J` of `R` and an `A`-module `N` with compatible `R`-action, the submodule
`J \cdot N` of `N` over `R` is in fact an `A`-submodule: the two scalar actions commute. -/
def smulTopOfTower (J : Ideal R) (N : Type*) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [Module A N]
    [IsScalarTower R A N] : Submodule A N where
  carrier := ((J • (⊤ : Submodule R N) : Submodule R N) : Set N)
  add_mem' hx hy := add_mem hx hy
  zero_mem' := zero_mem _
  smul_mem' a x hx := by
    change a • x ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N)
    refine Submodule.smul_induction_on (p := fun y => a • y ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N)) hx
      (fun r hr y _ => ?_) (fun y z hy hz => ?_)
    · rw [smul_comm a r y]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul hr Submodule.mem_top
    · rw [smul_add]; exact add_mem hy hz

@[simp]
theorem mem_smulTopOfTower (J : Ideal R) {n : N} :
    n ∈ smulTopOfTower (A := A) J N ↔ n ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N) :=
  Iff.rfl

omit [Module R M] [IsScalarTower R A M] in
/-- **A module on which the ideal acts by zero kills the base change.**  If every value of an
`A`-linear map `u : M ⟶ N` lies in `J \cdot N` for an ideal `J` of `R`, then the base change of
`u` to any `A`-module `C` on which `J` acts by zero vanishes. -/
theorem lTensor_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top {J : Ideal R} (u : M →ₗ[A] N)
    (h : ∀ m : M, u m ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N))
    (C : Type*) [AddCommGroup C] [Module A C] [Module R C] [IsScalarTower R A C]
    (hC : ∀ a ∈ J, ∀ c : C, a • c = 0) :
    LinearMap.lTensor C u = 0 := by
  refine TensorProduct.ext' fun c m => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.lTensor_tmul, LinearMap.zero_apply]
  refine Submodule.smul_induction_on (p := fun y => c ⊗ₜ[A] y = 0) (h m) (fun a ha n _ => ?_)
    (fun x y hx hy => ?_)
  · rw [← algebraMap_smul A a n, ← TensorProduct.smul_tmul, algebraMap_smul A a c, hC a ha c,
      TensorProduct.zero_tmul]
  · rw [TensorProduct.tmul_add, hx, hy, add_zero]

/-- **The ring-level core of Stacks 083K, for a base change to a module.**  If the target of an
`A`-linear map is flat over `R`, the base change of the map to an `R`-algebra `R'` vanishes, and
`C` is an `A`-module on which `\ker(R ⟶ R')` acts by zero, then the base change of the map to `C`
vanishes.

Geometrically: `Z = \Spec(R/\ker(R ⟶ R'))` is the closed subscheme of `S = \Spec(R)` of
Stacks 083K, `C` is the ring of an affine chart of `X ×_S Z`, and this is the vanishing of `u_Z`
on that chart. -/
theorem lTensor_eq_zero_of_rTensor_eq_zero [Module.Flat R N] (u : M →ₗ[A] N)
    (h : LinearMap.rTensor R' (u.restrictScalars R) = 0)
    (C : Type*) [AddCommGroup C] [Module A C] [Module R C] [IsScalarTower R A C]
    (hC : ∀ a ∈ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R'), ∀ c : C, a • c = 0) :
    LinearMap.lTensor C u = 0 :=
  lTensor_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top u
    ((rTensor_quotient_eq_zero_iff_forall_mem_smul_top (u.restrictScalars R)).1
      (rTensor_quotient_ker_eq_zero (R' := R') (u.restrictScalars R) h)) C hC

/-- **The finitely presented refinement of the ring-level core of Stacks 083K.**  If `M` is a
finite `A`-module, the target `N` is flat over `R`, and the base change of `u` to `R'` vanishes,
then there is a *finitely generated* ideal `J ⊆ \ker(R ⟶ R')` whose quotient already kills the
base change of `u`.

Geometrically: `Spec(R/J) ⟶ Spec(R)` is of finite presentation, `Spec(R') ⟶ Spec(R)` factors
through it, and the map becomes zero on it. -/
theorem exists_fg_ideal_rTensor_quotient_eq_zero [Module.Flat R N] [Module.Finite A M]
    (u : M →ₗ[A] N) (h : LinearMap.rTensor R' (u.restrictScalars R) = 0) :
    ∃ J : Ideal R, J.FG ∧ J ≤ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R') ∧
      LinearMap.rTensor (R ⧸ J) (u.restrictScalars R) = 0 := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (Module.finite_def (R := A) (M := M)).mp inferInstance
  -- a finitely generated ideal for each generator
  have key : ∀ z : M, ∃ J : Ideal R, J.FG ∧ J ≤ RingHom.ker (algebraMap R R') ∧
      u z ∈ J • (⊤ : Submodule R N) := by
    intro z
    exact exists_fg_le_ker_mem_smul_top (R' := R')
      (tmul_eq_zero_of_rTensor_eq_zero (u.restrictScalars R) h z 1)
  choose J hJfg hJle hJmem using key
  -- take the (finite) supremum of the ideals attached to the generators
  refine ⟨s.sup J, ?_, Finset.sup_le fun z _ => hJle z, ?_⟩
  · exact Finset.sup_induction Submodule.fg_bot
      (fun _ h₁ _ h₂ => Submodule.FG.sup h₁ h₂) fun z _ => hJfg z
  · refine rTensor_quotient_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_smul_top _ fun m => ?_
    have hspan : (⊤ : Submodule A M) ≤
        Submodule.comap (u : M →ₗ[A] N) (smulTopOfTower (A := A) (s.sup J) N) := by
      rw [← hs, Submodule.span_le]
      intro z hz
      exact Submodule.smul_mono_left (Finset.le_sup hz) (hJmem z)
    exact hspan (Submodule.mem_top) (x := m)

end Tower

end Stacks.Flattening

end
